From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PowerPhone Build <powerphone@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 07:25:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] audio: isolate and defer the legacy D0 transport

Frankel's sustained PCM0,D0 path is sensitive to both transaction geometry
and control ioctls. Put libtinyalsa-v1 behind a scalar-only shared-library
facade so its duplicate pcm_* symbols and incompatible object layout cannot
interpose on libtinyalsav2. Bind EP1 and open the legacy blocking PCM only
when the first complete client ring is already available, then submit whole
1,920-frame rings without mixer or SYNC_PTR traffic between writes.

Keep capture on the existing tinyalsav2 path and its qualified FIFO/3 worker,
while playback remains SCHED_OTHER. Give playback a four-ring framework queue
for scheduling margin and preserve fail-closed route ownership and xrun
accounting.
---
diff --git a/audio/aidl/default/Android.bp b/audio/aidl/default/Android.bp
index c21dc3c311..0f72e37812 100644
--- a/audio/aidl/default/Android.bp
+++ b/audio/aidl/default/Android.bp
@@ -212,6 +212,32 @@ cc_binary {
 // Opt-in research module for direct, exact-rate Frankel capture and PCM0,D0
 // speaker output. This is intentionally a separate IModule: it does not
 // replace the vendor primary module or register IConfig/effects.
+//
+// libtinyalsa and libtinyalsav2 export the same unversioned pcm_* API while
+// using incompatible private/public object layouts. Keep the old playback
+// transport in its own ELF, bind all of its internal calls locally, and export
+// only the scalar PowerPhone facade. This prevents either implementation from
+// interposing on the other inside the HAL process.
+cc_library_shared {
+    name: "libpowerphone_tinyalsa_v1",
+    vendor: true,
+    srcs: ["powerphone/LegacyTinyalsaV1.c"],
+    static_libs: ["libtinyalsa"],
+    shared_libs: ["libdl"],
+    export_include_dirs: ["powerphone/include"],
+    version_script: "powerphone/libpowerphone_tinyalsa_v1.map.txt",
+    ldflags: [
+        "-Wl,-Bsymbolic",
+        "-Wl,--exclude-libs,ALL",
+    ],
+    cflags: [
+        "-Wall",
+        "-Wextra",
+        "-Werror",
+    ],
+    stl: "none",
+}
+
 cc_binary {
     name: "android.hardware.audio.service-aidl.powerphone",
     relative_install_path: "hw",
@@ -231,6 +257,7 @@ cc_binary {
         "libbluetooth_audio_session_aidl",
         "liblog",
         "libmedia_helper",
+        "libpowerphone_tinyalsa_v1",
         "libstagefright_foundation",
     ],
     srcs: [
